{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["Scripture states regarding the plagues of houses: <b>\"and I will place a plague of tzara'at\"</b>, to hint that the hand of HaShem does this — it is not natural at all, as I have explained (Ramban on Leviticus 13:47). And it says, \"When you come to the land of Canaan, etc., in the house of the land of your inheritance,\" because He speaks to all Israel. Now it would have been fitting, after \"And HaShem spoke to Moses and to Aaron,\" that it say, \"Speak to the children of Israel,\" but Scripture abbreviates what is understood, or He speaks with them in place of all Israel, and it hints that the intention now is only to teach them all the laws of tzara'at, and that they should teach them to the priests. And Moses does not now admonish all Israel; rather, to those who enter the land He admonishes (Deuteronomy 24:8), \"Take heed in the plague of tzara'at, to observe very carefully,\" etc., for to them He commanded these laws from the outset."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:52.761407999Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}